<h3 id=3D"id-20251022MXCuBEAutomationWG-Agenda:">Agenda:&nbsp;</h3>
<ol>
<li>Definition of the output parameters from X-ray centering</li>
<li>The plan of the upcoming tasks</li>
</ol>
<h3 id=3D"id-20251022MXCuBEAutomationWG-Notes:">Notes:&nbsp;</h3>
<p>As an introduction the following slide was presented to open the discuss=
ion on the output. We already agreed on the input parameter as stated in th=
e figure. Thanks to Rasmus and Martin, MXLIMS now has a model for X-ray cen=
tering and especially for the volume to scan. (see <a class=3D"external-lin=
k" href=3D"https://github.com/rhfogh/mxlims_data_model/blob/main/ReleaseNot=
es.md" rel=3D"nofollow">https://github.com/rhfogh/mxlims_data_model/blob/ma=
in/ReleaseNotes.md</a>)</p>
<p><br></p>
<p><br></p>
<p><br></p>
<p><br></p>
<p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-manu=
al-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"false" heigh=
t=3D"262" src=3D"b4da3c335ca267631f30fdcde8bd0329" data-image-src=3D"/downl=
oad/attachments/177871717/image-2025-11-12_16-45-7.png?version=3D1&amp;modi=
ficationDate=3D1762962307500&amp;api=3Dv2" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D=
"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"177871722" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1=
" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-default-ali=
as=3D"image-2025-11-12_16-45-7.png" data-base-url=3D"https://confluence.esr=
f.fr" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-=
container-id=3D"177871717" data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"1" alt=
=3D"" width=3D"468"></span></p>
<p><br></p>
<p><u>Point 1</u></p>
<ul>
<li>From the volume to scan in the sample parameters, the X-ray centering d=
econvolutes 2D scans with different angle orientations.</li>
<li>From these 2D-scans, MXLIMS abstracts a 3D volume and sub-volumes with =
XYZ coordinates.</li>
<li>MXLIMS is implemented with the volume and sub-volume outputs as a list =
of point cloud to define all the samples that are on the sample support.</l=
i>
<li>Each point cloud (X, Y, Z) is model with a set of quality indicator.</l=
i>
<li>The set quality indicators needs to be defined to take advantage o. all=
 the capabilities available in the scoring program that would be used to an=
alyzed the images produced by the 2D-scans</li>
<li>The set of quality indicators should reflect the homogeneity of a singl=
e crystal and or the presence of multiple crystal on the same support.</li>
<li>The minimum set of quality indicator includes:
<ul>
<li>sum of intensities</li>
<li>number of spots</li>
<li>resolution</li>
<li>lattice meaning that the lattice at the position XYZ is equivalent to t=
he lattice at position X'Y'Z'</li>
</ul></li>
<li>The set of quality indicator can be later on expanded with new software=
 becoming available.&nbsp;</li>
<li>It would be better the model in MXLIMS is fully determined beforehand w=
ith all use cases instead of having a dictionnary (XML or JSON) that will b=
e filled up differently by each sites.</li>
<li>Processing of the images is done on a cluster that is not the machine r=
unning MXCuBE and the processing is launch on the fly and interdependently.=
 The X-ray centering should be able to launch different function with the m=
esh as an input and will be able to come back with position, centroid, etc =
as the site would prefer. This processing needs to be part of MX-CuBE and t=
he X-ray centering procedure</li>
<li>Rasmus offers to put up a survey to find out what is the minimum set of=
 quality indicators in all sites and the different sites will have to provi=
de what kind of quality indicator they use to do their X-ray centering. Als=
o if they use this as a tool for multi-crystal centering&nbsp;</li>
</ul>
<p><u>Point 2</u></p>
<ul>
<li><u>Abstract diffractometer is under development at ESRF. It should be u=
p and running by beginning of 2026</u></li>
<li><u>X-ray centering will be based on Abstract diffractometer</u></li>
<li><u>Processing will have to be further discussed for implementation unti=
l May 2026</u></li>
</ul>
<p><br></p>
<p><br></p>
<p><br></p>
    </div>
</body>
